The maximum possible area of $\triangle ABC$ is $\frac{1}{2}AC\cdot BP=\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{PA^2+PC^2}\cdot BP=\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{2^2+2^2}\cdot \frac{5}{2}=\frac{1}{2}\sqrt{8}\cdot \frac{5}{2}=\frac{1}{2}\cdot 2\sqrt{2}\cdot \frac{5}{2}=\frac{5}{2}\sqrt{2}=\boxed{15}$.

